        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-30991",
        ":question/problem": "Find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for $y=6({x}^{2}-cos\u2061x)+5.$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "We know that $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(cos\u2061x)=-sin\u2061x.$ Applying this formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6({x}^{2}-cos\u2061x)+5) \\\\  & =6\\cdot 2x+6sin\u2061x+0 \\\\  & =12x+6sin\u2061x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
