        ":question/problem": "Find the derivative of $y=\\frac{5sin\u2061x}{4}+\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}",
        ":question/worked-solution": "We know that $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(sin\u2061x)=cos\u2061x.$ Applying this formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{5sin\u2061x}{4}+\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}(cos\u2061x)+\\frac{1}{4}(4{x}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5cos\u2061x}{4}+{x}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
