        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-47985",
        ":question/problem": "Find the derivative of $y=-2cos\u2061x+{x}^{-2}.$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "We know that $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(cos\u2061x)=-sin\u2061x.$ Applying this formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-2cos\u2061x+{x}^{-2}) \\\\  & =-2(-sin\u2061x)+(-2){x}^{-2-1} \\\\  & =2sin\u2061x-2{x}^{-3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      }
